# User-approved 2026-09-08: utility-tab-expansion-boundary.
# Utility tab expansion boundary 001 through 008
Feature: Utility tab expansion boundary

  Background:
    Given the utility expansion base has Data Layer and Hotkeys workspaces
    And every existing executable check and consumer is recorded from that base

  # Utility tab expansion boundary 001
  Scenario: Utility tab expansion boundary 001
    When the reviewed host boundary is installed
    Then all existing executable checks and consumers remain represented
    And every changed shared path has an exact owner and installed observation
    And the preparation retains current and base evidence requirements
    And no all-runnable-pack feature gate is authorized

  # Utility tab expansion boundary 002
  Scenario: Utility tab expansion boundary 002
    Given the host boundary has architect-reviewed QA integration
    When the exact additive Probe tab contribution is planned from that QA base
    Then the plan contains the contribution owner, exact host consumers, prerequisites, and package proof
    And complete unrelated Data Layer feature families are absent from that plan
    And adding Probe requires no Data Layer implementation edit

  # Utility tab expansion boundary 003
  Scenario Outline: Utility tab expansion boundary 003
    Given a later contribution changes <shared_change>
    When the canonical planner evaluates its exact changed paths
    Then the plan retains <required_boundary>
    And the contribution does not receive an unconditional local-only exemption

    Examples:
      | shared_change                 | required_boundary                      |
      | shared utility lifecycle      | all declared lifecycle consumers       |
      | browser permissions           | conservative manifest verification     |
      | an unregistered shared path   | the missing-ownership stop             |

  # Utility tab expansion boundary 004
  Scenario: Utility tab expansion boundary 004
    Given a candidate changes ownership and consumes the narrower boundary in the same evidence range
    When canonical evidence requirements are derived
    Then the base owner and consumer requirements still apply
    And the candidate cannot use its own new mapping to omit those requirements

  # Utility tab expansion boundary 005
  Scenario: Utility tab expansion boundary 005
    Given the preparation still selects all runnable packs
    When its exact preflight completes
    Then the all-pack plan and causal paths are retained without launching those tasks
    And no global declaration or existing assertion is removed to force a bounded result
    And the task reports the conflict before expanding its implementation

  # Utility tab expansion boundary 006
  Scenario: Utility tab expansion boundary 006
    Given the host boundary and Probe contribution have architect-reviewed QA integration
    When only Probe private implementation changes and its exact evidence plan is derived
    Then the plan contains Probe checks and their mandatory prerequisites
    And complete Shell and unrelated Data Layer feature families are absent
    And every existing shared and terminal obligation remains registered

  # Utility tab expansion boundary 007
  Scenario: Utility tab expansion boundary 007
    Given the same Probe implementation and utility checks run in standalone and hosted pages
    When their focused evidence is compared
    Then the report separates common utility tasks from additional host tasks
    And every additional task observes the declared host boundary or a mandatory prerequisite
    And recorded durations separate recurring host overhead from one-time preparation
    And a lower pack count alone is not accepted as proof of lower development cost

  # Utility tab expansion boundary 008
  Scenario: Utility tab expansion boundary 008
    Given an additive utility plan selects fewer than all packs but includes complete unrelated feature families
    When the expansion route is assessed for completion
    Then the preparation remains incomplete with the exact causal plan retained
    And unrelated broad verification and repair work is not launched to complete that route
    And existing assertions remain registered under their actual owners
